{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And El Shaddai give you mercy.</b> What did Jacob see to bless them with El Shaddai? To teach you how many sufferings came upon Jacob: while he was still in his mother's womb, Esau quarreled with him, as it is said: ״ויתרוצצו הבנים בקרבה״, and they said that they were quarreling over the inheritance of two worlds. When he went outside, Esau sought to kill him, as it is said: ״על רדפו בחרב אחיו״. He fled from him to the house of Laban — see how many troubles he had there: ״הייתי ביום אכלני חורב״ etc. He left the house of Laban; Laban pursued him — he escaped from him. Esau came to kill him, and he lost all that gift that he had brought him — he escaped from him. The trouble of Dinah came upon him; afterward, the trouble of Rachel. After all these troubles, he sought to dwell in tranquility, as it is said: ״וישב יעקב״ — immediately the trouble of Joseph came upon him; afterward, the trouble of Simeon; afterward, the trouble of Benjamin. And thus he says: ״לא שלותי ולא שקטתי ולא נחתי ויבא רוגז״. Therefore he said: now, He who said to the world 'enough' when He created it — let Him say to my troubles 'enough.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:02.335783086Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}